INT. SKI PATROL HUT - SUMMIT - NIGHT

A cedar-lined cabin clinging to a ridge. Frost patterns bloom on the windows. A woodstove glows orange. Skis in racks, avalanche probes in a barrel, a first-aid sled by the door. Wind presses against the walls.

THORVALD EKLUND, 50s, patrol chief, weathered, beard crusted with ice, pours coffee at the stove. ELOISE MAKINDE, 30s, a doctor in a red jacket, adjusts a radio. KAMAU NJOROGE, 20s, rookie patroller, laces a boot. ISADORA VANCE, 40s, a guest in a designer parka, sits by the stove with a thermos, her gloves still on.

The mood is warm. Sleepy. A deck of cards lies half-dealt on the table.

THORVALD
Last run's clear. We close at ten.

KAMAU
Big storm tomorrow?

THORVALD
Big one.

ISADORA
I can't believe you let me stay. I'm grateful.

ELOISE
You were stuck.

ISADORA
I was lost.

KAMAU
You were on the wrong side of the ridge.

ISADORA
Somebody put the sign in the wrong place.

THORVALD
Nobody touched the sign.

ISADORA
Then it fell.

The radio crackles.

NANDI (V.O.)
Base to summit. Come in, summit.

Eloise lifts the handset.

ELOISE
Summit.

NANDI (V.O.)
Doctor, I need a headcount.

ELOISE
Four in the hut. Thorvald, me, Kamau, and a guest.

NANDI (V.O.)
A guest?

ELOISE
Lost skier. Isadora Vance.

Silence on the line. Static. The stove ticks. Thorvald sets down his coffee.

NANDI (V.O.)
Doctor. The only Isadora Vance on the lift manifest checked out at noon.

ELOISE
Say again?

NANDI (V.O.)
She went down at noon. She's in the bar.

Isadora's smile doesn't change. The thermos in her lap clicks as she turns the lid.

KAMAU
Maybe there's two.

THORVALD
There's not two.

ISADORA
There is, actually.

She stands. Her glove slips. Beneath it: a wrist wrapped in a hospital bracelet, the name blacked out.

ISADORA (CONT'D)
I'd hoped to rest longer.

ELOISE
Who are you?

ISADORA
The woman who didn't make it down.

Thorvald draws the avalanche probe from the barrel. Kamau backs against the wall. Eloise drops the handset. It swings on its cord.

ISADORA (CONT'D)
(gentle)
Thorvald. Eleven years ago. The east chute.

His knuckles go white on the probe.

THORVALD
(hoarse)
You were dead.

ISADORA
And you were the one who dug.

The wind drops. The stove goes out.
